==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|la|grc|ἀμφορεύς||[[two-]][[handled]] [[pitcher]], [[unit]]s of [[liquid measure]]}}. As a Roman unit, originally an elision of {{m|la|amphora quadrantal}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|amphora}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|amphora<1>|gen_pl=amphorum/amphorārum}}

# {{lb|la|chiefly|_|historical}} [[#English|amphora]], {{ngd|a large vessel, especially one made of clay with two handles used for storing and transporting wine}}
# {{lb|la|historical}} [[#English|amphora]], {{ngd|a Roman unit of liquid measure equivalent to about 26 L}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|la|unit of liquid measure}} {{l|la|quadrantal}}, {{l|la|amphora quadrantal}}

